      "benefit": "CI",
      "years": [2021, 2022],
      "pattern": "shock",
      "direction": "increase",
      "magnitude": "~+0.35 A/E versus local baseline; 2021-22 average A/E 1.284 vs 2016-2020 average 0.931 and 2023-24 average 0.941; excess claims ~835",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "evidence": [
        "artifacts/ae_ci_by_year.csv: 2020 AE=0.880, 2021=1.273, 2022=1.295, 2023=0.937, 2024=0.944",
        "artifacts/ae_ci_by_year.csv: 2021-22 is an abrupt, flat-topped elevation relative to both the preceding 2016-2020 level and the 2023-24 reversion",
        "CI year-to-year A/E dispersion is materially overdispersed versus Poisson, so this is described as a level excursion rather than Poisson z-score flags"
      ],
      "recommended_action": "Investigate 2021-2022 CI claims by diagnosis, age/gender, underwriting/coding, exposure and expected-claim build; determine whether this reflects a genuine one-off level shift, data/coding issue, or model miscalibration; if confirmed, follow up pricing/valuation for the affected window and continue monitoring the 2023-2024 reversion."
    }
  ]
}

